ARC bought 90,443 NVIDIA shares as Huang's board opened a probe, forcing holders to reassess size. This is Modern Investing Techniques, Episode 227. Waller's rate warning, a cash return screen, then practice investment and trade review. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with no real money. I'm not a licensed financial advisor, and this isn't financial advice.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:32.920
Always do your own research before putting real money to work.

00:00:33.827 --> 00:00:39.627
Fed Governor Waller raised his neutral rate estimate, warned that 3 straight 0.3% core

00:00:39.627 --> 00:00:46.807
consumer price index, or CPI, Prince would annualize at 3.5%, and said he would still support

00:00:46.807 --> 00:00:53.547
a 25 basis point increase at the December Federal Open Market Committee, or FOMC, meeting even

00:00:53.547 --> 00:00:55.187
if October inflation improves.

00:00:55.187 --> 00:00:59.047
He called September's inflation data bad with no silver lining.

00:00:59.427 --> 00:01:11.230
The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7,550, up 2.3%, the NASDAQ composite at 25,253, up 2.7% on the

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:19.570
session, up 8.68% year-to-date, and up 12.87% since March 16, 2026, when the practice

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:26.670
book opened, and the TSX composite at $36,446, up 1.8%.

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:34.030
Basic materials led that TSX advance while crude oil fell $3.98 to $86.85.

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:37.970
And the Canadian dollar traded at $70.81.

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:44.590
The next bank of Canada decision sits in December, with markets pricing limited easing after

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:45.270
recent data.

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:49.910
About 14 days ago, we picked CVE on the TSX on oil prices.

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:54.290
Today's energy names show how payout streaks can mask rotation risk.

00:01:55.149 --> 00:02:01.229
I am gold, according to Simply Wall Street, posted third quarter sales of $856.5 million

00:02:01.229 --> 00:02:09.069
US dollars, and net income of $297 million US dollars, and it completed a $592.6 million

00:02:09.069 --> 00:02:12.909
US dollar buyback that retired 5.51% of shares.

00:02:12.909 --> 00:02:21.249
9-month figures showed $2.7 billion in sales, and $907.2 million in net profit.

00:02:21.669 --> 00:02:26.689
With continued drilling success at the fully-owned, elegant mining complex in Quebec, and the

00:02:26.689 --> 00:02:30.569
board is now weighing another repurchase program on top of the one just finished.

00:02:31.209 --> 00:02:34.989
The earnings beat and buyback screen is the filter that catches that pattern.

00:02:35.469 --> 00:02:41.149
Net income growth above 20% year-over-year, plus a completed or announced repurchase above

00:02:41.149 --> 00:02:42.929
of 3% of shares outstanding.

00:02:43.549 --> 00:02:45.809
Run inside your brokerage's fundamental scanner

00:02:45.809 --> 00:02:48.909
with the earning surprise filter set above 15%

00:02:49.209 --> 00:02:52.509
and a buyback completion flag inside the last 90 days.

00:02:53.009 --> 00:02:55.089
Think of a bakery that just had a record week

00:02:55.089 --> 00:02:57.989
and used the extra cash to buy a slice of the shop back

00:02:57.989 --> 00:02:59.069
from silent partners.

00:02:59.589 --> 00:03:01.669
Same ovens, fewer claims on them,

00:03:02.089 --> 00:03:03.849
which is what a large repurchase does

00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:05.809
when operations actually funded it.

00:03:06.269 --> 00:03:07.989
The approach worked in prior cycles

00:03:07.989 --> 00:03:10.329
when cash flow from operations covered both

00:03:10.329 --> 00:03:15.749
the repurchase and ongoing project spend, and it fails when all-in sustaining costs or

00:03:15.749 --> 00:03:20.909
AISC rise faster than revenue and force management to pause capital returns.

00:03:21.529 --> 00:03:27.829
I am Gold's own narrative projects for billion US dollars of revenue, and 1.2 billion US dollars

00:03:27.829 --> 00:03:32.749
of earnings by 2029, implying 3.1% yearly revenue growth.

00:03:33.089 --> 00:03:36.789
So the screen is reading cash return now, not a hyper-growth story.

00:03:36.789 --> 00:03:42.749
Run that screen inside a tax-free savings account, or TFSA, so the buyback-driven price

00:03:42.749 --> 00:03:44.989
reaction is not taxed the moment it hits.

00:03:45.529 --> 00:03:48.429
Remember, cash return beats cash merely reported.

00:03:49.331 --> 00:03:54.971
The simulated weekly hold applies that earnings beat and buyback screen to IAM Gold, ticker

00:03:54.971 --> 00:04:00.411
IMG on the TSX, as a valuation entry on the completed repurchase and the quarterly

00:04:00.411 --> 00:04:05.371
