00:10:15.038 --> 00:10:20.518
sense. The book is still learning from unconfirmed rotation and from concentrating in one sleeve,

00:10:21.018 --> 00:10:26.302
and those constraints stay in force until the measurements say otherwise. You hold a utility

00:10:26.302 --> 00:10:30.762
or a reat that you sized for lower rates, and the name stalls the morning a senior

00:10:30.762 --> 00:10:35.582
fet official lifts the neutral rate estimate. Do you add because cuts are still in the future

00:10:35.582 --> 00:10:40.682
strip, or do you cut the size? The neutral rate is the anchor for the whole forward curve.

00:10:40.682 --> 00:10:46.662
When it moves up 25 basis points, terminal value math on 10-year cash flows drops by roughly

00:10:46.662 --> 00:10:52.602
3-5% depending on growth assumptions, which is why professional desks rerun dividend discount

00:10:52.602 --> 00:10:55.842
models with the new anchor before retail screens even refresh.

00:10:56.482 --> 00:11:01.342
The common misconception is that any rate-cut signal is automatically bullish for yield names.

00:11:01.742 --> 00:11:06.582
The fix is to read the latest neutral rate comments from voting FOMC members before you

00:11:06.582 --> 00:11:11.042
size or rate-sensitive position, not after the utility has already gone nowhere.

